    {
      "id": "pQgxkag0ksUZUV6ROIcbR",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 4967.568683329783,
      "y": 4466.737514329917,
      "width": 2840.60205078125,
      "height": 3997.5,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "cx4WX",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 157930212,
      "version": 7019,
      "versionNonce": 1920147088,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1790039639906,
      "created": 1789639556690,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "1. generate data\n2. transfer it to reconciliation engine using http/sftp (rather than disk import)\n    - sftp is not wired???\n3.1 do the complete reconciliation process and create episodes\n3.2 simultaneously if the generated data has come through as a tpa = qualified, then:\n        - it is sent to FABRIC\n        - fabric looks up the episode type for track a or b\n        - chooses the beacon template\n        - forms the request \n        - sends it to beacon and gets a response --> not yet wired & cant bcoz we dont have production beacon, right????\n\n4. assuming beacon verified and hence we eventuallly got the payment - reconciliation engine checks the payments and marks episodes wherever required\n\n\n\n\n\nQuestions:\n- are the \"not built\" parts correct?\n- but isnt sftp/http implementation done for us to talk to Verify and craneware - not for importing docs\n- is reconcillation engine part of fabric??? - i know its not supposed to be but how is it built\n\n\n\n*************************\n\n- why arent they turned on??? is it because we dont have their docs, or something else??? - BE HONESTa\n- what are vendor modules? - what all do you need for this: system decision, just need to write code ??\n- so based on the shapes, does sftp import lie in fabric/connectors/ ???\n- what are we importing via sftp right now??, generated data right?? -- what are we supposed to import???\n\n\n**************\n\n1. FOR the famous task of pulling data from tables to check the type between track a and track b && choosing a beacon template, \nis this task completely done by reconcillation engine OR completley by fabric OR there is a split?\n\n2. so you are saying that we can build it and point to our mock (which is the complete aim of the prototype)??? \n    - if so they ask me the exact question that you want ---> I can answer a simple thing as well:\n    - that, the doc 2 takes priority in building stuff --> just wanted to put this in so you remember --> else you can ask your question\n\n3. link and build the vendor modules needed for our system to work - do you not have data shape for verity and craneware\n\n4. wire the file generation in correctly in the initial seed as well as the regenerate data options\n\n5. give me a list of things that we just found through all this discussion which are remaining -->\nWE NEED TO BUILD IT NOW AS I CANT MESS UP THIS INTERVIEW --> hence give me a list of things and blockers from me\n\n\n***********\n\n1. for doc 1 we had 6 files generated --> what has changed?? does it still work in same way\n    - orchestrator gives main keys - individual genrators genrate records\n    - instead of 4 --> hoe many gener8s now?\n    - instead of 6 --> how many files generated now???\n\n2. did you use beacon sdk function for template or just went raw code based on docs?\n    - review and if possible use sdk functions because that just make it more easy for us\n    - also use the actual docs website to search and get things instead of relying on our dumbass local copy\n\n3. have we mocked beacons data as well??\n\n4. the basic data generated based on doc 1 - are we sending it to reconcilation engine using http or just file imports like before\n\n5. What does becaon even retrun right now?\n    - mock responses?\n    - what are the responses?\n    - do we have a defined shape of those responses based of docs??\n    - are we handling them??\n    - are we changing/updating episodes based of that data??\n\n\n***** \n\n1. so ore those 15 new files fot verity, cranware and beacon their moch records?? - who generated these?\n    - via a generator script or you yourself?\n\n2. are we sure which \"BEACON\" service are we supposed to use- since you listed 2 of them?\n3. based on the new templates - do he have the code setup?\n\n4. \"Currently 44 of 57 Beacon fields are INVENTED. The retrieved templates would move most of them to sourced.\" --> what does this mean wrt mock data??\n\n5. Beacon stuff:\n    - from the newly found templates - do you still dont have the shape of responses??\n    - according to our system is beacon supposed to induce anychange in the episodes\n        - eg: get data from beacon to fabric and then fabric updates episode - (i think this needs to be done, correct me if I am wrong)\n    - mak sure the data connectors and generators are basedo ut of actual response shapes\n    - I am even OKAY IF YOU WRITE THE MOCK DATA YOURSELF WITHOUT ANY GENERATOR SCRIPT - SINCE I NEED TO SHOW THAT THE Beacon is working - ALSO i dont want you to spend time on creating scripts\n\n*****\n\n1. on the Beacon page of document 2, page number 3, at the end there is a sentence. The last sentence of the page says, \"Public Evidence Review,\" and in that it says:\n- Beacon FAQ\n- partner tokens\n- partner permissions\n- pharmacy template\nAll of them go to support.beaconchannelmanagement.com and that tells us which beacon we are supposed to use, right?\nMy question is: are we really using the same beacon templates and the same beacon SDKs and docs everywhere????\n\n2. Make a detailed plan for getting all the templates and response shapes and then build it completely -- https://support.beaconchannelmanagement.com/en/collections/11972931-using-beacon-rebate-model\n\n\nADMIN INSTRUCTIONS:\n1. Nothing about Beacon should be self-created other than data. The templates, the responses, everything should be according to the functions. Everything should be according to the documentation. \n2. implement the logic where consuming beacon msgs will update episode --->>>> beacon -> fabric -> episode update \n3. remember my \"create mock data using claude\" advice --> BUT THE FORMAT SHOULD BE THE ONE FROM DOCS\n4. you can also open docs in browser and search for yourself - https://support.beaconchannelmanagement.com/en/\n\n*****\n\nQuestions:\n1. does fabric do some of the reconcilation part - updating episode details in DB\n    - we might need a common module which does these tasks --> we can call that module in recon.. and favric as awell\n\n2. do i need to process the mock data in the same way from beacon ?\n\n\n\n\n\n\n***********\n",
      "fontSize": 26,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "1. generate data\n2. transfer it to reconciliation engine using http/sftp (rather than disk import)\n    - sftp is not wired???\n3.1 do the complete reconciliation process and create episodes\n3.2 simultaneously if the generated data has come through as a tpa = qualified, then:\n        - it is sent to FABRIC\n        - fabric looks up the episode type for track a or b\n        - chooses the beacon template\n        - forms the request \n        - sends it to beacon and gets a response --> not yet wired & cant bcoz we dont have production beacon, right????\n\n4. assuming beacon verified and hence we eventuallly got the payment - reconciliation engine checks the payments and marks episodes wherever required\n\n\n\n\n\nQuestions:\n- are the \"not built\" parts correct?\n- but isnt sftp/http implementation done for us to talk to Verify and craneware - not for importing docs\n- is reconcillation engine part of fabric??? - i know its not supposed to be but how is it built\n\n\n\n*************************\n\n- why arent they turned on??? is it because we dont have their docs, or something else??? - BE HONESTa\n- what are vendor modules? - what all do you need for this: system decision, just need to write code ??\n- so based on the shapes, does sftp import lie in fabric/connectors/ ???\n- what are we importing via sftp right now??, generated data right?? -- what are we supposed to import???\n\n\n**************\n\n1. FOR the famous task of pulling data from tables to check the type between track a and track b && choosing a beacon template, \nis this task completely done by reconcillation engine OR completley by fabric OR there is a split?\n\n2. so you are saying that we can build it and point to our mock (which is the complete aim of the prototype)??? \n    - if so they ask me the exact question that you want ---> I can answer a simple thing as well:\n    - that, the doc 2 takes priority in building stuff --> just wanted to put this in so you remember --> else you can ask your question\n\n3. link and build the vendor modules needed for our system to work - do you not have data shape for verity and craneware\n\n4. wire the file generation in correctly in the initial seed as well as the regenerate data options\n\n5. give me a list of things that we just found through all this discussion which are remaining -->\nWE NEED TO BUILD IT NOW AS I CANT MESS UP THIS INTERVIEW --> hence give me a list of things and blockers from me\n\n\n***********\n\n1. for doc 1 we had 6 files generated --> what has changed?? does it still work in same way\n    - orchestrator gives main keys - individual genrators genrate records\n    - instead of 4 --> hoe many gener8s now?\n    - instead of 6 --> how many files generated now???\n\n2. did you use beacon sdk function for template or just went raw code based on docs?\n    - review and if possible use sdk functions because that just make it more easy for us\n    - also use the actual docs website to search and get things instead of relying on our dumbass local copy\n\n3. have we mocked beacons data as well??\n\n4. the basic data generated based on doc 1 - are we sending it to reconcilation engine using http or just file imports like before\n\n5. What does becaon even retrun right now?\n    - mock responses?\n    - what are the responses?\n    - do we have a defined shape of those responses based of docs??\n    - are we handling them??\n    - are we changing/updating episodes based of that data??\n\n\n***** \n\n1. so ore those 15 new files fot verity, cranware and beacon their moch records?? - who generated these?\n    - via a generator script or you yourself?\n\n2. are we sure which \"BEACON\" service are we supposed to use- since you listed 2 of them?\n3. based on the new templates - do he have the code setup?\n\n4. \"Currently 44 of 57 Beacon fields are INVENTED. The retrieved templates would move most of them to sourced.\" --> what does this mean wrt mock data??\n\n5. Beacon stuff:\n    - from the newly found templates - do you still dont have the shape of responses??\n    - according to our system is beacon supposed to induce anychange in the episodes\n        - eg: get data from beacon to fabric and then fabric updates episode - (i think this needs to be done, correct me if I am wrong)\n    - mak sure the data connectors and generators are basedo ut of actual response shapes\n    - I am even OKAY IF YOU WRITE THE MOCK DATA YOURSELF WITHOUT ANY GENERATOR SCRIPT - SINCE I NEED TO SHOW THAT THE Beacon is working - ALSO i dont want you to spend time on creating scripts\n\n*****\n\n1. on the Beacon page of document 2, page number 3, at the end there is a sentence. The last sentence of the page says, \"Public Evidence Review,\" and in that it says:\n- Beacon FAQ\n- partner tokens\n- partner permissions\n- pharmacy template\nAll of them go to support.beaconchannelmanagement.com and that tells us which beacon we are supposed to use, right?\nMy question is: are we really using the same beacon templates and the same beacon SDKs and docs everywhere????\n\n2. Make a detailed plan for getting all the templates and response shapes and then build it completely -- https://support.beaconchannelmanagement.com/en/collections/11972931-using-beacon-rebate-model\n\n\nADMIN INSTRUCTIONS:\n1. Nothing about Beacon should be self-created other than data. The templates, the responses, everything should be according to the functions. Everything should be according to the documentation. \n2. implement the logic where consuming beacon msgs will update episode --->>>> beacon -> fabric -> episode update \n3. remember my \"create mock data using claude\" advice --> BUT THE FORMAT SHOULD BE THE ONE FROM DOCS\n4. you can also open docs in browser and search for yourself - https://support.beaconchannelmanagement.com/en/\n\n*****\n\nQuestions:\n1. does fabric do some of the reconcilation part - updating episode details in DB\n    - we might need a common module which does these tasks --> we can call that module in recon.. and favric as awell\n\n2. do i need to process the mock data in the same way from beacon ?\n\n\n\n\n\n\n***********\n",
