      "seed": 242948784,
      "version": 2459,
      "versionNonce": 1933617776,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1790047687716,
      "created": 1790039445606,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "- are we understanding the rebate model correct based on latest changes\n- show the beacon templates used\n- can we show the ASSUMED mock templates for verity and craneware?\n- ARE WE STILL USING tpa.json --> or have we wired in the logic where we:\n    1. use verity and cranware data that (created using tpa.json) in our completer flow\n    2. does our reconcillation engine work with that --> do we have that logic where our engine processes data in both ways\nand that too from fabric(connector layer) and database, in order to make correct episode updates?\n- can we have list of all these A-xx, B-xx, C-xx tags that are being used\n- so in total there are 6 ways in which records get handled by reconcilation engine? --> 4 lead to data being PARKED -- 2 create an episode -- x lead details to be appended to episode\n- why does pb, and tpa need to communicate --> i though reimbursement and rebate tracks were completely independent in working?\n- is 18 basically the number of if rules that we apply?\n\n- doesnt the reconcillation engine also write records into PARKED tables and stuff when their matching details are not available?\n- why do we have groundtruth --- doe sit have just the values created by orchestration and not by generators afterwards - how is it used?\n- as we label each legal combo from tree, doe that mean we have 372 different tags? -- also does each combo have only one legal tag\n\n## POINTS TO REMEMBER\n\n- fecthing and interpreting data are 2 different jobs\n- The reconciliation engine takes one episode plus a point in time and returns a verdict.\nIt cannot write to a source record; it only appends a new verdict row.\n- 4224 legal combinations --> 372 verdict pairs\n- pharmacy and medical benefits have diff files to show client and server data --> 340b path has all combined in tpa.json\n- 50 if else rules - 43 track predicts(reimbursement & rebate) - 7 cross track escalation",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "- are we understanding the rebate model correct based on latest changes\n- show the beacon templates used\n- can we show the ASSUMED mock templates for verity and craneware?\n- ARE WE STILL USING tpa.json --> or have we wired in the logic where we:\n    1. use verity and cranware data that (created using tpa.json) in our completer flow\n    2. does our reconcillation engine work with that --> do we have that logic where our engine processes data in both ways\nand that too from fabric(connector layer) and database, in order to make correct episode updates?\n- can we have list of all these A-xx, B-xx, C-xx tags that are being used\n- so in total there are 6 ways in which records get handled by reconcilation engine? --> 4 lead to data being PARKED -- 2 create an episode -- x lead details to be appended to episode\n- why does pb, and tpa need to communicate --> i though reimbursement and rebate tracks were completely independent in working?\n- is 18 basically the number of if rules that we apply?\n\n- doesnt the reconcillation engine also write records into PARKED tables and stuff when their matching details are not available?\n- why do we have groundtruth --- doe sit have just the values created by orchestration and not by generators afterwards - how is it used?\n- as we label each legal combo from tree, doe that mean we have 372 different tags? -- also does each combo have only one legal tag\n\n## POINTS TO REMEMBER\n\n- fecthing and interpreting data are 2 different jobs\n- The reconciliation engine takes one episode plus a point in time and returns a verdict.\nIt cannot write to a source record; it only appends a new verdict row.\n- 4224 legal combinations --> 372 verdict pairs\n- pharmacy and medical benefits have diff files to show client and server data --> 340b path has all combined in tpa.json\n- 50 if else rules - 43 track predicts(reimbursement & rebate) - 7 cross track escalation",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
